    <h1>Mini Biography: Elon Musk</h1>
    <p>Elon Musk is a businessman and engineer known for leading companies in the electric vehicle, space, and technology industries.</p>

    <h2>Early Life</h2>
    <p>He was born in Pretoria, South Africa, and later moved to Canada and then the United States to pursue his education and career.</p>

    <h2>Important Achievement</h2>
    <p>He played a <strong>key role in building SpaceX, the first private company to send astronauts to the International Space Station</strong>.</p>
    <p>He is remembered as a <em>driving force behind Tesla</em> for helping push electric cars into the mainstream car market.</p>
    <p>One trait that made him stand out was <mark>his willingness to take big risks on new technology</mark>.</p>

    <h2>Correction Corner</h2>
    <p><s>He founded Tesla.</s> He actually joined Tesla as an early investor and chairman shortly after it was founded, then later became CEO.</p>

    <h2>Interesting Examples</h2>
    <p>SpaceX rockets like the Falcon 9 can land back on Earth after launch, reusing stages instead of throwing them away.</p>
    <p>Tesla's Model 3 became one of the best-selling electric cars, helping normalize electric vehicles for everyday drivers.</p>

    <h2>Words That Inspire</h2>
    <p>He once said, <q>When something is important enough, you do it even if the odds are not in your favor.</q></p>
    <blockquote>
      Failure is an option here. If things are not failing, you are not innovating enough.
    </blockquote>

    <h3>My Reflection</h3>
    <p>I find Elon Musk interesting because his companies show how ambitious goals in engineering can push entire industries forward.</p>

